WEBVTT

00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:05.405
A dbt project is a folder.

00:00:05.685 --> 00:00:15.641
Models, seeds, tests and macros live in their own subfolders, and one file at the top, dbt_project.yml, gives the project its name and settings.

00:00:16.591 --> 00:00:20.535
A second file, profiles.yml, says where dbt runs.

00:00:20.815 --> 00:00:25.612
Our profile has one target, dev, and it points at a DuckDB database file.

00:00:26.562 --> 00:00:27.855
First, the database.

00:00:28.135 --> 00:00:31.550
On the home screen, click New Connection, and choose DuckDB.

00:00:32.815 --> 00:00:34.557
Name it nyc taxi dev.

00:00:34.837 --> 00:00:40.624
For the file, type a path next to your projects folder: nyc taxi dev dot duckdb.

00:00:40.904 --> 00:00:44.683
DuckDB creates the file the first time dbt connects.

00:00:44.963 --> 00:00:45.563
Save.

00:00:46.513 --> 00:00:47.584
Now the project.

00:00:47.864 --> 00:00:52.295
Go back home, open the DBT Project card, and click New Project.

00:00:54.867 --> 00:00:56.405
Call it nyc taxi.

00:00:56.685 --> 00:01:01.945
Keep the template folders switched on, pick the nyc taxi dev connection, and save.

00:01:04.487 --> 00:01:06.705
Studio creates the folder and opens it.

00:01:06.985 --> 00:01:10.582
Here are the template folders, and the two files we just talked about.

00:01:11.532 --> 00:01:21.714
Open dbt project dot yml: the project name is nyc taxi, it uses the profile with the same name, and lists where each kind of file lives.

00:01:22.664 --> 00:01:25.398
Let's check that dbt can reach the database.

00:01:25.678 --> 00:01:30.333
In the command box under the terminal, type dbt debug, and press Enter.

00:01:31.838 --> 00:01:36.303
dbt finds the project and the profile, and connects to DuckDB.

00:01:36.583 --> 00:01:37.677
All checks passed.

00:01:38.627 --> 00:01:47.072
Before the first commit, add a dot gitignore file at the top of the project, so build output, logs, data and the database stay out of git.

00:01:48.325 --> 00:01:52.472
And a short README, so people who open the repository know what it is.

00:01:59.718 --> 00:02:05.078
Now create an empty repository on GitHub: the plus button, then New repository.

00:02:06.028 --> 00:02:11.374
Name it nyc taxi dbt, and make it public, so anyone can get the code.

00:02:11.654 --> 00:02:13.498
This rehearsal copy is private.

00:02:13.778 --> 00:02:16.891
Add no README, gitignore or license, and create it.

00:02:17.841 --> 00:02:22.008
Copy the HTTPS address of the new, empty repository.

00:02:22.958 --> 00:02:27.277
Back in Studio, open the Git tab, and click Initialize Repository.

00:02:29.519 --> 00:02:35.810
Stage all the changes, type a message, create the nyc taxi dbt project, and commit.

00:02:38.763 --> 00:02:39.943
Click Publish Branch.

00:02:40.223 --> 00:02:44.371
Studio asks for the remote: paste the repository address, and add it.

00:02:44.651 --> 00:02:46.891
Studio pushes the main branch to GitHub.

00:02:47.841 --> 00:02:49.696
Refresh the repository page.

00:02:49.976 --> 00:02:55.311
The project is on GitHub: the folders, the two YAML files, the gitignore, and the README.

00:02:56.261 --> 00:03:05.856
To recap: a DuckDB connection, a dbt project called nyc taxi, a passing dbt debug, and the first commit on GitHub.

00:03:06.136 --> 00:03:09.268
From now on, every lesson ends with a commit and a push.

00:03:09.548 --> 00:03:10.806
Next, we get the data.
